 "start": 158, "end": 226, "text": "It is a two-story, brick, Georgian-revival house built in c.1920-24."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847:d03", "start": 227, "end": 247, "text": "It was a home of Dr."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847:d03", "start": 248, "end": 274, "text": "Edgar McCurry (1877-1962)."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847:d03", "start": 275, "end": 367, "text": "It is located on the north side of Howell Street near its intersection with Franklin Street."}, "D4S8": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847:d03", "start": 368, "end": 410, "text": "It was designed by architect Willis Irwin."}, "D4S9": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847:d03", "start": 411, "end": 503, "text": "Its NRHP nomination identified it as the only example of Georgian Revival style in Hartwell."}, "D4S10": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847:d03", "start": 504, "end": 556, "text": "The listing included a second contributing building."}, "D4S11": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847:d03", "start": 557, "end": 625, "text": "There is also a \"McCurry House\" included in the Benson Street-Forest"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847:d04", "start": 0, "end": 199, "text": "82°56′22″W ﻿ / ﻿ 34.354618°N 82.939431°W ﻿ / 34.354618 ; -82.939431 Area 1 acre ( 0.40 ha ) Built 1920 Architect Willis Irwin Architectural style Georgian Revival MPS Hartwell MRA NRHP reference No ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847:d04", "start": 200, "end": 291, "text": "86002035 [ 1 ] Added to NRHP September 11 , 1986 The McCurry-Kidd House , located at 602 W."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847:d04", "start": 292, "end": 302, "text": "Howell St."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0201-5c8cecac2847: